# Testing and Debugging for Game Development

## Context
- When developing complex game mechanics that need to be verified
- When working on a team where code quality must be maintained
- When adding new features to existing game systems
- When tracking down elusive bugs or performance issues
- When ensuring consistent behavior across different devices and browsers

## Requirements
- Create a comprehensive testing strategy with unit, integration, and end-to-end tests
- Use test-driven development for core game mechanics
- Implement in-game debugging tools for real-time inspection
- Create performance monitoring and profiling utilities
- Add debug visualization for physics, collisions, and game state
- Design code for testability through dependency injection and modular architecture
- Implement proper logging with severity levels for production diagnostics
- Build automated test pipelines to catch regressions early

